  "raw": {
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Energy-Manager--Energy-Division_R-05012-2": {
      "title": "Energy Manager, Energy Division",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nDepartment Energy Job Posting Title Energy Manager, Energy Division Job Description The Energy Manager position involves the use of specialized skills in HVAC controls, medium voltage 15KV, peaking generation, wind turbines, and associated switchgear, including electric meters. Monitors the organization’s energy use, develop strategies to reduce energy use and demand. Maintains and completes energy audits for university owned buildings. Purchases natural gas and watches markets to develop strategies to minimize financial losses. Be proficient with Tridium Niagara N4 control system, design control logic, trouble shoot control related issues, design and build control panels, do field installs of control related parts. This position reports to the Director of Energy Management. PERKS: Benefits package with Heath, Prescription, Dental & Vision Insurance Accrues 6.77 hours vacation and 3.7 hours sick leave per pay period earn up to 272 hours of paid leave per year, (176 vacation, 96 sick leave) State paid holidays New Year’s Day, MLK Day, Memorial Day, Juneteenth National Independence Day, Independence Day, Labor Day, Veterans Day, Thanksgiving & Christmas Tuition Assistance - day one eligibility for the employee, their spouse and dependents Employees are eligible for up to 6 credit hours per semester. Retirement KBOR 403(b) Mandatory 5.5% employee contributions, 8.5% employer contributions If you have contributed to a retirement for a minimum of 1 year within the past 5 years at a KPERS employer, state employer or institution of higher education, you may be eligible for immediate participation . Benefits : To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits . Salary: $27.00/ hour Minimum Qualifications: This position requires a high-school diploma or GED equivalency and three years of experience with Niagara N4 software, 15KV generation, wind turbines, and switchgear. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree, in related fields Energy manager certification 5 or more years of experience in HVAC controls and 15KV equipment Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Develop energy audits for campus buildings Purchase natural gas, follow markets Review of electric rate tariffs Evaluate peaking and wind performance, make changes as required Review of electric usage and peak demand of campus facilities Complete EIA860 and EIA923 federal forms Maintain electric meter server and meters Trouble shoot and program VFDs Maintain 15KV switches and gas pressures Operate 15KV breakers as required Check and make adjustment to wind turbine operation Trouble shoot PLC controllers for generation and switchgear facilities Maintain fault protection relays Develop logic control programming for HVAC control equipment Install HVAC control equipment Design and build HVAC control enclosures Commission and troubleshoot control issues Create graphics for control system Design Lon and BacNet MSTP, IP, ModBus communication networks Do plan take offs for ordering control parts Maintain network switches for HVAC equipment Maintain buildings system control server, update software, trouble shoot application errors Being proficient with Tridium Niagara N4 Respond to power outages and control related issues after hours Must be able to lift/carry 50lbs Must be able to climb ladders Priority Deadline: Screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  Appointment Date: Start date to be determined after acceptance of an offer and completion of a criminal background check. Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted. Required Application Documents :  Applicants must submit a current resume and the names and contact information of three professional references. Applicant documents should be submitted in one PDF. If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Keith Dreher, Search Committee Chair kjdreher3@fhsu.edu 785.628.5281 Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Instructional-Designer--Teaching-Innovation-and-Learning-Technologies_R-05197-1": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer, Teaching Innovation and Learning Technologies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nDepartment Innovative Learning Strategies Job Posting Title Instructional Designer, Teaching Innovation and Learning Technologies Job Description The Department of Teaching Innovation and Learning Technologies (TILT) at Fort Hays State University seeks an Instructional Designer whose work centers on one question: how do we create human connection in digital spaces? That question is the north star of FHSU's Digital Master Plan, and this role is where it becomes practice in courses. The Instructional Designer partners with faculty to design courses and learning experiences — online, hybrid, and in person — in which instructor presence, peer interaction, and student agency are designed for rather than left to chance. The role requires expertise across TILT’s portfolio of instructional design, educational technology, and faculty development. The Instructional Designer's work supports FHSU's strategic commitment to student success, informs how the university evaluates and adopts learning technologies, and helps faculty make sound judgments about where AI and other tools strengthen learning and where they displace the relationships learning depends on. The position reports to the Director of Innovative Learning Strategies and is on campus in Hays, Kansas. Key responsibilities: Course and learning design Partner with faculty to design and redesign courses, modules, activities, and assessments that incorporate Regular and Substantive Interaction across online, hybrid, and face-to-face formats Guide faculty through course development from concept to delivery, including alignment of outcomes, activities, and assessment Apply quality course assurance frameworks that treat connection and presence as design outcomes, not by-products Faculty development Design and deliver workshops, consultations, and resources that help faculty grow as course designers, in collaboration with TILT's faculty development team Support faculty in making informed, principled decisions about AI in their courses: where it extends what students can do, and where it substitutes for the thinking and interaction in the course Contribute to TILT's programming and communities for faculty as they are developed Educational technology Help evaluate and make recommendations for learning tools and platforms to meet pedagogical criteria Support faculty adoption of approved tools, including the LMS, with attention to accessibility and student engagement Learning data and quality Help faculty read and design based their own course data Contribute to ongoing quality improvement in online and blended learning, including regular and substantive interaction standards Document design decisions and outcomes so TILT's work is visible and can inform institutional priorities Minimum qualifications: Master's degree in education, instructional design, educational technology, or a related field or six years of experience in lieu of degree Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain design and technology choices to non-technical audiences Expertise with course quality assurance frameworks, such as SUNY Online Course Quality Review Rubric (OSCQR), Online Learning Consortium (OLC) Scorecard, Quality Matters Working familiarity with a learning management system (FHSU uses Blackboard Learn) Strong technical aptitude and a demonstrated ability to learn new tools and concepts quickly Preferred qualifications: Two or more years of experience in instructional design or educational technology in higher education Demonstrated experience with project management and the ability to coordinate communication with several faculty at once and meet deadlines Online or hybrid teaching experience in higher education Familiarity with presence-based frameworks for course design, such as the Community of Inquiry model, and the ability to apply them in consultation with faculty Experience helping faculty use generative AI in ways that preserve instructor–student and peer interaction rather than replace it Experience interpreting course-level data (engagement, activity, outcomes) in partnership with instructors Working knowledge of accessibility standards for digital learning (WCAG, Universal Design for Learning) and of regular and substantive interaction expectations for online courses Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with faculty and colleagues across disciplines and backgrounds Experience designing or facilitating faculty professional development Background and experience with open educational resources (OERs) adoption and development We welcome applications from candidates who do not meet every preferred qualification but show sound judgment about learning, a clear point of view on technology, and a strong willingness to grow in the role. Benefits : To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits . Appointment Date: Start date to be determined after acceptance of an offer and completion of a criminal background check.   Priority Deadline: November 12, 2026. Screening of complete applications will begin immediately following the priority deadline and will continue until the position is filled.   Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted.   Required Application Documents :  Applicants must submit a current resume. References may be requested from final candidates later in the hiring process. Highly Preferred Application Documents: Cover Letter & Design Philosophy - A letter of application that outlines your qualifications and shares your learning design philosophy. In particular, we invite you to reflect on: How you determine learning intent and select instructional methods or tools Your approach to consulting and partnering with faculty How you organize and manage multiple concurrent projects How you use evidence or data to solve problems and evolve your practice Your approach to universal design and accessibility for diverse learners Applicant documents should be submitted in one PDF. If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Dr. Andrew Feldstein, Search Committee Chair apfeldstein@fhsu.edu 785.628.4788 Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Assistant-Professor-of-Accounting--Department-of-Economics--Finance--and-Accounting_R-05200-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting, Department of Economics, Finance, and Accounting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nDepartment Economics, Finance & Accounting Job Posting Title Assistant Professor of Accounting, Department of Economics, Finance, and Accounting Job Description The Department of Economics, Finance, and Accounting at Fort Hays State University invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track faculty position in accounting. Fort Hays State University is a teaching focused institution, and the primary mission of the Department of Economics, Finance, and Accounting is to provide quality instruction. We seek applicants who have a passion for teaching and challenging students in the classroom and in the online environment. This is an on-campus position located in Hays, Kansas. Minimum Qualifications : PhD or DBA candidates in a related field with 18 graduate hours in accounting coursework. Accounting coursework must include significant work with U.S. GAAP. Preferred Qualifications : Conferred PhD or DBA with a concentration/specialization in accounting OR individuals at ABD status who are within one year of completing the degree. The CPA credential is preferred. Preference will also be given to applicants with teaching experience (both on-campus and online) Responsibilities : This is a nine-month, tenure-track position. The candidate accepted for this position will be expected to teach 12 credit hours per semester in accounting (may include both on-campus and online courses). We seek applicants with a willingness to teach a variety of accounting courses, undergraduate or graduate, on-campus or online, as needed by the department. The selected candidate will stay current in the field through scholarly activity and will also participate in departmental, college, and university activities. Rank : Assistant Professor Appointment Date : August 2027 Salary: Faculty salaries are 90% of current College and University Professional Association (CUPA) averages by rank and discipline. Benefits : To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits . Priority Deadline : The priority deadline is January 8, 2027. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted. Required Application Documents : Applicants must submit the following: Cover letter specifying how the applicant’s credentials match the job description and how they meet the minimum and preferred qualifications. Current curriculum vitae or professional resume University transcripts (unofficial are acceptable) showing all graduate coursework Contact information for three professional references Applicant documents should be submitted in one PDF file . If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Ms. Jessica Heronemus-Claiborn, Search Committee Chair jaheronemus@fhsu.edu (785) 628-4746   About the Department : The Department of Economics, Finance, and Accounting is one of four departments in the Robbins College of Business and Entrepreneurship at FHSU and offers outstanding undergraduate and graduate instruction in the accounting, economics, and finance disciplines. Currently, the degrees and majors offered by the department are a BBA in Accounting; a BBA in Accounting with a concentration in public accounting, a BBA in Finance, a BBA in Finance with concentrations in banking, economics, and financial planning, a BBA in International Business and Economics; and a BBA in Financial Forensics and Fraud Investigation. Minor programs in accounting, economics, finance, banking, and international business and economics, and certificate programs in accounting, banking, economics, finance, and insurance are also offered. Website: http://www.fhsu.edu/efa / About the College : Mission: The Robbins College of Business and Entrepreneurship at Fort Hays State University offers highly engaging educational experiences, preparing and supporting our students and alumni for professional success in a dynamic, global environment.  Our focus is on instructional engagement. Faculty add value to student instruction and the community through scholarly activity and ongoing professional engagement. The College provides service that benefits the university, our disciplines, and the greater community. ( Adopted by COBE Faculty on May 4, 2016). Description: The college consists of four large and growing departments:  Applied Business Studies; Economics, Finance, and Accounting; Computer Science and Informatics; and Management and consists of more than 50 full-time faculty supported by key staff.  In addition to a wide range of undergraduate programs, it has a significant sized Master of Business Administration program and also offers Master of Professional Studies degrees in Human Resource Management and varying areas of Computer Science and Informatics. On-campus students majoring in these academic areas number approximately 800 and domestic distance learning students number 1370. The COBE is housed in the historic, but recently remodeled McCartney Hall and newly constructed Hammond Hall. In addition to on-campus offerings, the college offers several undergraduate and graduate degrees online. It also participates in joint degrees with two partners universities in China. Among the college’s many unique attributes is the Dane G. Hansen Entrepreneurship Scholarship Hall which opened with the 2016-2017 academic year. Website:  http://www.fhsu.edu/rcob/ . Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Grounds-Equipment-Operator-Specialist--Physical-Plant-Grounds_R-05201-1": {
      "title": "Grounds Equipment Operator Specialist, Physical Plant/Grounds",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nDepartment Horticulture Job Posting Title Grounds Equipment Operator Specialist, Physical Plant/Grounds Job Description An Equipment Operator Specialist maintains, repairs, and utilizes heavy-duty vehicles and equipment to care for the University grounds. This role involves using equipment to perform various duties, including waste disposal, mowing, landscaping, irrigation, greenhouse maintenance, and snow removal. The specialist operates sanitation trucks, recycling trucks, dump trucks, front-end loaders, backhoes, tractors, and other large motor vehicles.   Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent. One year of relevant experience. Valid driver's license.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience operating heavy-duty equipment (sanitation trucks, mowers, skid steers, high lifts, back hoes, trenchers, etc.). Experience in groundskeeping, horticulture, or greenhouse management. Experience in maintaining and operating irrigation systems. Experience in applying chemicals.   Responsibilities: Operate and maintain sanitation trucks and recycling trucks. Retrieve, empty, and return trash and recycling containers at campus facilities. Operate a hydraulic dumping system. Operate large mowers, tractors, skid-steer loaders, high lifts, trenchers, and backhoes to maintain campus grounds and complete landscaping projects. Mow, trim, and edge lawns and grass areas. Plants, water, weed, and prune trees, shrubs, flowers, and lawns. Apply fertilizers, herbicides, pesticides, and other chemicals according to safety guidelines. Perform pre-operational checks and minor repairs to heavy-duty machinery. Assist with tree removal. Assist with snow removal for sidewalks, streets, and parking lots. Assist with irrigation installation and maintenance. Execute maintenance required to keep vehicles or equipment in working order. Manage the safety, quality, and cleanliness of work areas to maintain a suitable work environment. Take preventive measures to avoid injury to workers or other persons and damage to equipment and property. Ensure that all operations use proper equipment to maintain health and safety standards   Salary : $15.91 per hour   Benefits : To view FHSU's competitive benefits package visit FHSU Benefits .   Application Deadline: Review of applicants will begin November 19, 2026 and continue until the position is filled.   Appointment Date : Start date will be determined after acceptance of an offer and background check clearance.   Application Process: To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted.   Required Application Documents: Applicants should submit a resume.   If you have questions regarding this position, please contact: Cody Norton cjnorton@fhsu.edu 785-628-4038 Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Athletic-Event---Facility-Operations-Specialist_R-05204-1": {
      "title": "Athletic Event & Facility Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nDepartment Gross/Cunningham Hall Complex Operations -A Job Posting Title Athletic Event & Facility Operations Specialist Job Description The Athletic Events and Facilities Specialist is an entry-level position reporting to the Athletic Events & Facilities Operations Manager and assists with maintaining & preparing facilities to ensure a safe, clean, & professional environment for student-athletes, staff, & spectators. This role includes routine facility maintenance, cleaning, & equipment operation, as well as setup, preparation, & teardown for athletic competitions, tournaments, practices, & special events. Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: 1-2 years of Facility or Event experience Experience operating various cleaning and maintenance equipment, including, but not limited to: high-speed floor buffer, carpet extractor, floor auto scrubber, and field sweeper. Salary: $15.03 per hour Shift Options: Monday - Friday 6:00am - 2:30 pm Monday - Friday 10:00am - 6:30 pm plus shift differential Monday - Friday 2:00pm - 10:30 pm plus shift differential Application Priority Deadline:  Screening of complete applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Benefits : To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits . Perks:  KBOR 403B retirement plan Benefits package with Dental & Vision Paid Time Off – earned every two weeks Accrues 6.77 hours vacation Accrues 3.7 hours sick leave State paid holidays New Year’s Day, MLK Day, Memorial Day, Independence Day, Juneteenth, Labor Day, Veterans Day, Thanksgiving & Christmas Tuition Assistance for you and your family - DAY ONE ELIGIBILITY Employees are eligible for up to 6 free credit hours per semester. Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted. Required Application Documents: Applicants must submit a resume. Responsibilities: Maintain and prepare collegiate athletic facilities, including stadiums, arenas, practice fields, courts, weight rooms, locker rooms, and support areas, to ensure a safe, clean, and welcoming environment for student-athletes, staff, and fans. Provide on-site support during collegiate athletic events, tournaments, and practices to troubleshoot facility issues and ensure a positive experience for athletes, staff, and fans. Assist with all aspect of set-up, teardown and post-event cleanup, returning facilities to game-ready and daily-use condition efficiently and safely. Provide general laundry support for several different areas . Install audio-visual equipment, including PA systems and scoreboards. Set up signage, banners, and branding for events, including sponsor and university materials. Support crowd management by ensuring pathways, exits, and seating areas are safe and accessible. Perform exterior maintenance, including snow removal, debris clearance, and preparation of fields and courts for practices and competitions. Replace light bulbs and perform minor repairs to maintain safe and functional athletic environments. Perform general upkeep and maintenance of floors, walls, carpets, windows, and furniture to uphold university and athletic department standards. Safely operate and maintain equipment such as auto floor scrubbers, carpet extractors, high-pressure washers, high-speed floor buffers, and vacuums. Dust, clean, and maintain furnishings and surfaces in offices, locker rooms, meeting spaces, and common areas. Sweep, mop, vacuum, and shampoo floors and carpets as needed, including high-traffic areas used by student-athletes and spectators. Clean and sanitize restrooms according to established procedures and restock dispensers to support large-scale events. Lift and carry items up to 50 lbs. safely, including athletic equipment, event supplies, and furniture. Perform additional duties as assigned to support the success of the athletic department and events. Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Financial-Aid-Advisor--Office-of-Financial-Aid_R-05196-1": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Advisor, Office of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nDepartment Financial Aid Job Posting Title Financial Aid Advisor, Office of Financial Aid Job Description This position is responsible for supporting the Federal Workstudy and Kansas Career Workstudy programs, various federal and state grant programs, and other financial aid processes. The employee in this position reports to the Director of Financial Assistance. The successful candidate will be detail-oriented and accurate with the ability to work within a highly technical PC and mainframe based computing environment. They will also exhibit strong critical thinking, written and oral communication skills, be self-motivated and able to motivate others. Additionally, the candidate will demonstrate a willingness to contribute to a team-oriented environment. This position is an on-campus position located on the campus of Fort Hays State University in Hays, KS.   Minimum Qualifications : Bachelor’s Degree or four years of professional experience in lieu of degree. One year of professional experience in a student affairs or student personnel setting   Preferred Qualifications : Master’s Degree or six years professional experience in lieu of degree. Experience working with financial aid Supervisory experience Experience working in a university setting Knowledge FERPA or other federal, state, and university regulations Experience working with Workday   Appointment Date: The start date will be determined after acceptance of an offer and successful completion of a background check.   Application Deadline : November 3, 2026. Review of applications will begin after the priority deadline and continue until the position is filled.   Benefits: To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits . Salary : $39,644   Responsibilities : Manage the Federal Workstudy (FWS) Program, including determining student eligibility, managing the waitlist, and monitoring workstudy earnings for federal program compliance. Manage the Kansas Career Workstudy (KCWS) Program, including determining student eligibility, monitoring earnings, and completing yearly Kansas Board of Regents report. Assist with Pell Grant processing, including monitoring recalculations, lifetime limits, and reconciliation. Coordinate the processing of TEACH Grants, including eligibility determination and exit counseling. Process consortium agreements, including communicating with students and schools and adjusting awards. Assist with the Satisfactory Academic Progress processes. Communicate with students and families regarding various financial aid and student employment processes. Serve as a financial aid eligibility counselor for a portion of the alphabet as assigned by the Director. Supervise, directly or indirectly, student employees within the Office of Financial Assistance. Assist with the communication plan for the Office of Financial Assistance in the creation of Workday student engagement plans and messages, print publications, and website updates. Advise student and families on financial aid processes, especially FWS eligibility. Present to student groups/parents at university events, Financial Aid Nights, and other events as assigned by the Director, including some nights and weekends. Perform other office management functions as needed or assigned by the Director.   Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted.   Required Application Documents : Applicants must submit a resume. A cover letter and names and contact information for three professional references are recommended.   Applicant documents should be submitted in one PDF.   If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Chantelle Arnold csarnold@fhsu.edu  (785) 628-4408 Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Chair--Department-of-Agriculture_R-05195-1": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Agriculture",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nDepartment Werth College of Science, Technology & Mathematics Job Posting Title Chair, Department of Agriculture Job Description Fort Hays State University (FHSU) is seeking applicants for Chair of the Department of Agriculture. The position is a 12-month appointment. Depending on qualifications, applicants will be evaluated for tenure and the rank of Full Professor upon hire.  The successful candidate must have a distinguished record of teaching, research, and service with an understanding and appreciation for on-campus and online delivery systems. The Chair will also have excellent communication and organizational skills, have demonstrated leadership abilities, and understand the needs of faculty, staff, and students.  Future directions for the Department will include conservation and precision agriculture, renovation of the agriculture education program, and explorations of new undergraduate and graduate degree offerings and certifications.   Minimum Qualifications : Earned doctorate in agriculture or closely-related field; A recent record of the items listed below in keeping with appointment to Full Professor: - Teaching excellence; - Commitment to student success; - Research accomplishments; - Service to the discipline and community.   Preferred Qualifications : Successful academic administrative experience including both fiscal and supervisory responsibilities, especially within the field of agriculture; Demonstrated success with student recruitment and retention initiatives; Experience with formalized assessment; Record of external funding through grants and/or donor fundraising; Demonstrated success with online education.   Responsibilities The Chair of the Department of Agriculture reports to the Dean of the Werth College of Science, Technology, and Mathematics. The Chair, in consultation with the Dean, is responsible for the management, operation, and development of the department, including:   Provide strategic direction and vision for the department. Oversee curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement considering holistic student success initiatives and program review. Ensure programs meet regulatory requirements. Support innovation in teaching, research, and service activities. Foster interdisciplinary collaboration across departments and colleges. Recruit, hire, onboard, mentor, and evaluate faculty members including merit reviews. Manage promotion, tenure, and post-tenure review processes. Coordinate faculty workloads and teaching assignments including course scheduling. Encourage faculty scholarship, grant activity, and professional development. Address personnel issues, conflicts, and performance concerns. Monitor enrollment trends and student retention. Address student concerns and academic issues. Assist with student recruitment and outreach activities. Manage the department budget and other financial resources; Lead student recruiting and retention efforts for the department; Teach 6 credit hours per semester and 3 credit hours during the summer. Initiate and facilitate donor fundraising; Ensure department initiatives align with University and Regents goals and plans; Participate in college and university service activities;   Rank: Preferred:  Professor; Will consider:  Associate Professor   Benefits : To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits .   Appointment Date: July 2027.  This position is an on-campus position , not eligible for remote assignments.   Priority Deadline : Review of applicants will being on or after November 4, 2026 and continue until the position is filled.   Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted.   Required Application Documents Candidates should submit a single PDF containing: Cover letter addressing experience, qualifications, and how the applicant is suited to the position; Current curriculum vitae; The names and contact information of at least three professional references.   If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Dr. Mark Arant mearant@fhsu.edu   About the Department : The Department of Agriculture has eight full-time faculty positions serving approximately 400 undergraduate students pursuing Bachelor of Science degrees in Agriculture or Agricultural Business with the latter available online. The Agriculture major includes options in Agricultural Education, Agronomy, Animal Science, Agricultural Leadership, Agricultural Communications, Business Agronomy, and General Agriculture. A partnership with the FHSU Robbins College of Business and Entrepreneurship resulted in a new “4+1” MBA program with an agriculture emphasis that launched in 2022. Teaching and research are supported by a 3,400-acre University Farm, which reports to the Werth College Dean’s Office. See www.fhsu.edu/agriculture for additional information.   About the College : The Werth College of Science, Technology, and Mathematics was formed in 2015 by bringing together the departments of Agriculture, Applied Technology, Biological Sciences, Chemistry, Computer Science, Geosciences, Mathematics, and Physics. The college employs approximately 70 full-time faculty, 1250 undergraduate majors, and 50+ graduate students. It also makes significant contributions to the university’s General Education program and to the Kansas Academy of Mathematics and Science, which is an early-college program for high-achieving high-school students. Undergraduate students participate in technical, classroom, field, and lab experiences that many schools would reserve for graduate students. Our academic programs are innovative and our facilities are outstanding. The Werth College of Science, Technology, and Mathematics teachers embrace a one-on-one teaching and mentoring philosophy and provide robust research opportunities for our students. Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Professional-Academic-Advisor--Robbins-College-of-Business-and-Entrepreneurship_R-05189-1": {
      "title": "Professional Academic Advisor, Robbins College of Business and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nDepartment Robbins College of Business & Entrepreneurship Job Posting Title Professional Academic Advisor, Robbins College of Business and Entrepreneurship Job Description The Professional Academic Advisor provides comprehensive, student-centered academic advising that promotes student success, retention, persistence, and timely degree completion. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, and campus partners, the advisor supports students in navigating academic requirements, educational planning, university policies, and available resources. The advisor employs a holistic and developmental advising approach while utilizing student success technologies and data-informed practices to enhance student outcomes. Enhancement for University Alignment The Professional Academic Advisor utilizes a holistic, developmental, and student-centered approach to advising that empowers students to make informed decisions, achieve their educational goals, and develop the skills necessary for lifelong learning and career success.   Appointment: Full-Time, 12-Month Position Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from a regionally accredited institution or four years of experience in lieu of degree. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree from a regionally accredited institution or six years of experience in lieu of degree. Experience in academic advising, student affairs, higher education, or a related field. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of best practices in holistic and developmental academic advising. Understanding of student development theory and student success principles. Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to actively listen and respond effectively to student needs. Ability to build and maintain positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as a collaborative team member. Proficiency in using student information systems, advising technologies, and data to support student success initiatives. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Academic Advising and Student Success Provide academic advising through multiple delivery methods, including in-person, virtual, phone, and electronic communication. Assist students in developing academic plans that support degree completion and career goals. Support student persistence and timely graduation through advising, advocacy, intervention, and data-informed decision-making. Monitor student academic progress using reports, alerts, and other student success tools. Conduct proactive outreach to students regarding academic standing, registration, retention initiatives, and university resources. Promote student engagement and involvement in academic and co-curricular opportunities. Assist students with major exploration, academic planning, and navigation of university processes. Student Support and Advocacy Identify student needs and connect students with appropriate campus resources and support services. Advocate for student success while maintaining professional boundaries and institutional standards. Assist with academic reinstatement and other student success initiatives as appropriate. Interpret and communicate university, college, and Kansas Board of Regents (KBOR) policies, procedures, and academic regulations. Collaboration and Campus Engagement Advise students across the disciplines and demographic populations represented within the College and University. Collaborate with faculty, administrators, and campus partners to support student success initiatives. Provide guidance to faculty and administrators regarding curriculum requirements, degree progression, scheduling, and time-to-completion considerations. Participate actively in new student orientation programs, retention initiatives, recruitment activities, and college events. Contribute to a positive and student-focused advising culture within the College. Records, Reporting, and Professional Development Utilize student success and academic information systems to maintain accurate advising records and documentation. Prepare and maintain reports related to advising outcomes, student progress, and retention efforts. Maintain current knowledge of university curricula, degree requirements, policies, and procedures. Participate in professional development opportunities and remain informed of emerging trends and best practices in academic advising. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the mission of the College and University.   Salary and Benefits : Bachelor’s degree - $36,000 per year (12-month contract). Master’s degree or higher - $39,000 per year (12-month contract).   To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits .   Appointment Date: Start date to be determined after acceptance of an offer and completion of a criminal background check.   Priority Deadline: October 30, 2026. Screening of complete applications will begin immediately following the priority deadline and will continue until the position is filled.   Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted.   Required Application Documents :  Applicants must submit a current resume. Applicant documents should be submitted in one PDF.   If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Melissa Hunsicker Walburn, Search Committee Chair mjhunsickerwalburn@fhsu.edu Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Assistant-Professor--Department-of-English-and-Modern-Languages_R-05186-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Department of English and Modern Languages",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nDepartment English and Modern Languages Job Posting Title Assistant Professor, Department of English and Modern Languages Job Description Minimum Qualifications : PhD in English with concentration in Pre-1865 American literature (in hand by August 2026). Evidence of successful teaching experience required, including First-Year Writing. Ability and willingness to teach online. Preferred Qualifications: Additional subspecialties or interests to expand course offerings of department Experience of successful online teaching, and/or experience with advising student organizations preferred. Responsibilities : Fort Hays State University faculty on tenure track perform their duties on a 60% instruction, 20% scholarship, and 20% service division of labor with a 4/4 semester load. Teaching responsibilities for this position will include American literature surveys, upper-division and graduate literature courses, general education literature courses, and composition, both on-campus and online. Summer teaching is possible. Rank:   Assistant Professor, Tenure-Track Appointment Date: August 2027 Application Deadline: Review of applicants will begin October 29, 2026. Benefits : To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits . Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted. Required Application Documents:   Applicants must submit the following materials: Cover letter detailing their experience and qualifications Current c.v. Statement of teaching philosophy, evidence of teaching excellence (to include but not limited to course evaluations, peer observations, and syllabi) Copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts Names and contact information for three professional references. Applicant documents must be compiled and submitted in ONE PDF. If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Dr. Eric Leuschner, Chair edleuschner@fhsu.edu 785-628-4285 About the Department: The Department of English and Modern Languages at Fort Hays State University offers a Bachelor of Arts in English with three concentrations: Literature, Teaching, and Writing; a Bachelor of Arts in Spanish in two concentrations: Spanish Education and Spanish for Specific Purposes; and a Master of Arts degree in English. Most programs are offered both on-campus and online. The Department has been an integral part of the university’s international programs, offering our Composition sequence in cross-border programs in China for over twenty years. We envision our graduate concentration as important training for similar careers in teaching academic writing internationally. In addition, the department offers courses in the general education program including the first-year composition sequence, interdisciplinary courses, and modern languages. About the College: The College of Arts, Humanities, and Social Science's mission: Preparing students for successful professional lives, lifelong learning, and civic engagement in a rapidly changing world by cultivating critical thinking, social scientific inquiry, creative problem-solving, effective communication, and innovative leadership  For more information about the college, please visit https://www.fhsu.edu/cahss/ . Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Assistant-Professor--Department-of-Music---Theatre_R-05190-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Department of Music & Theatre",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nDepartment School of Visual and Performing Arts - Music & Theatre Job Posting Title Assistant Professor, Department of Music & Theatre Job Description Music and Theatre, in the School of Visual and Performing Arts at Fort Hays State University, Hays, Kansas, invites applications for a full-time, 9-month tenure-track position beginning August 2027.  We seek an engaging artist-teacher of violin and viola who will teach lessons, string pedagogy, string techniques, and mentor music education students in preparation for teaching careers.  A student-centered focus on pedagogy, mentoring, and program growth and development is required.  Duties also include performing a principal role in the Hays Symphony, assisting with orchestra sectionals, and providing leadership in string section development.  Additional duties may be assigned based on the needs of the program and the candidate’s qualifications.   The successful candidate will be expected to engage in the community and region to recruit students, advocate for the performing arts and music education, and successfully network with music education professionals in regional high schools and community colleges.  FHSU is a hub for Music Education in the western Kansas region, with special attention on rural program development and placement.  A focus on rural music education development and advocacy is essential to the success of the program.    FHSU Music and Theatre is committed to building a community of collaborative teacher-artists with diverse skills from a multitude of backgrounds.  Music Education is a primary focus for the program.  FHSU Music and Theatre treats community-engaged work in teaching, scholarship, and/or service as legitimate and important areas of faculty activity, of comparable value to high-impact classroom teaching and mentorship, the scholarship of discovery, and the scholarship of teaching and learning. Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Music (violin or viola performance, string pedagogy, music education, or related field), or a Masters in Music with equivalent professional experience, commensurate to advanced graduate studies in Music. Experience teaching applied violin/viola at the collegiate level, private studio, and/or in the public schools.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of success in recruiting/retaining applied violin and viola students. Strong record of pedagogical engagement with music education programs. Expertise in string pedagogy.   Rank: Assistant Professor of Music.   Benefits : To review our competitive benefit package, please visit FHSU Benefits . Appointment Date: August 12, 2027 Application Deadline : Screening of applications will begin October 29, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Application Process : To apply for this position, please visit FHSU Careers . Only electronic applications submitted through the webpage will be accepted.   Application Deadline : Screening of applications will begin after November 1 and continue until the position is filled.   Required Application Documents :  Cover letter that addresses the candidate’s skills and qualifications for this position, no more than two pages in length. Curriculum Vitae. Names and contact information for three professional references that can speak to teaching and performance abilities. Links to performance and teaching demonstration videos.  Teaching videos should demonstrate both violin and viola.   Applicant documents should be submitted in one PDF. If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Prof. Benjamin Cline Chair, Music and Theatre brcline@fhsu.edu    About the Program : Music and Theatre, in the School of Visual and Performing Arts, consists of 15 full-time-faculty and offers B.M. degrees in Music Education, Music Performance, and Music Composition, and B.A. in Music.  The program offers a wide variety of performances to the public including music theatre, opera, instrumental and vocal ensembles, chamber music, the Tiger Marching Band, the Hays Symphony, theatrical performances, and faculty artist and guest artist recitals. The program is housed in Malloy Hall, consisting of two rehearsal halls, a theatre, several classroom spaces, practice rooms, and faculty studios.  We are committed to expanding access to students in the region and around the globe. For more information visit https://www.fhsu.edu/music-and-theatre/     School of Visual and Performing Arts Mission Statement: The School of Visual and Performing Arts is a vibrant and diverse artistic community that fosters and inspires the creative potential of students, cultivating their artistic visions for the future as they prepare for meaningful and successful lives in the arts. We promote and respect creativity, expression, and diversity in all its forms.     School of Visual and Performing Arts Vision Statement: The School of Visual and Performing Arts is dedicated to advancing human creativity and inspiring students to be change-makers within their communities.  Community of Hays FHSU is located in Hays, a vibrant college town of approximately 20,000, located halfway between Kansas City and Denver on Interstate 70. Hays is the regional center for education, health care, professional services, shopping, culture, and recreation for the western half of Kansas. The community boasts excellent recreational programs and facilities, including the comprehensive Center for Health Improvement, Hays Aquatic Park, Smoky Hill Country Club, Hays Municipal Golf Course, and extensive walking, running, and biking trails. Hays is within 45 minutes of two large lakes that offer great opportunities for boating, fishing, and camping. The Hays Municipal Airport provides connecting service to Denver with several flights daily. The Hays community is home to excellent Pre-K and K-12, public and private schools. With over 60 restaurants, major retail outlets, a low unemployment rate, and very short commute times, the city provides a safe, welcoming, low-cost, high-quality living environment for the residents who call \"Hays, America\" home. Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you."
    },
    "https://fhsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/CAREERS/job/FHSU-Main-Campus-Hays-Kansas/Professional-Academic-Advisor--Werth-College-of-Science--Technology--and-Mathematics_R-05185-1": {
      "title": "Professional Academic Advisor, Werth College of Science, Technology, and Mathematics",
